Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 04:19:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1076/1198] A broken score stops the run before the music
 (1087); floors as fuses: a score not under 200 tokens, the music not under
 750, locked against stray edits, every knob in bounds (1088); the music half
 together under a shared ceiling, Plan clears an old score (1089)

The engine judges the score the AR wrote: M:, L:, K: present and clean, Q: a tempo, never three colons in a row
(calibrated on the studio's takes: 20 whole, every broken one caught). The page explains in plain words: why,
which adapters weighed on the music half, how far past their limits, and the shared ceiling measured on the
takes (whole up to 2.25 together, broken from 2.5).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
